# Components, data and assets

## Component ownership

| Component | Home | Behavior / rendering | Implementation priority |
|---|---|---|---|
| EssayShell / PostLayout | Article route | Owns primary pane, flow intro rail and sticky companion boundary | P0 |
| HeroFrontispiece | Entry primary pane | Editorial art, responsive crop, separate OG image | P0 |
| EssayHeader / RevisionNote | Entry primary pane | Real metadata; one low-weight revision disclosure | P0 |
| ExecutiveSignal / AuthorCard | Entry rail; compact mobile flow | Never sticky, never included in focus layouts | P0 |
| SectionMarker | Each major article section | Stable ordinal + current left rule; linked to outline state | P0 |
| ReadingCompanion | Article rail | One orientation owner; nearby outline + dock + optional authored note | P0 |
| ContextualNote | Article rail / inline mobile | Static authored mapping; manual disclosure/dismissal | P1 |
| ThreadScene | Primary pane at six anchors | Canonical text/image/status; real link to focus route | P0 |
| ThreadDock | Inside ReadingCompanion | Follow/hold preview; user collapse wins | P1 |
| ThreadFocus | Shared focus renderer | Selected beat; details, figure and limits | P0 |
| RunningExampleCard | ThreadFocus rail only | Known artifact metadata; unknown fields explicit or omitted | P0 |
| ThreadOverview | ThreadFocus rail; mobile navigation | Six real scene links; no article TOC | P0 |
| EvidenceFocus | Shared focus renderer | Full evidence set / selected receipt | P0 |
| ReceiptDisclosure | Essay summary / EvidenceFocus | Native details; finding and scope always visible | P0 |
| EvidenceGuide / ReceiptIndex | EvidenceFocus rail only | Evidence classes and source navigation | P0 |
| Figure / FigureViewer | Inline + shared overlay host | Exact art, caption, long description, return context | P0 |
| MediaSplit / InlineAside | Defined prose block | Partial primary width, stacks when narrow | P0 |
| EditorialTable | Main or focus pane | Semantic table; local horizontal overflow when needed | P0 |
| EvidenceLabel / ImplementationStatus | Relevant claims/records | Class and maturity kept separate | P0 |
| BoundaryGrid / ManagedVariation | Main pane | Distinct explanatory comparisons, not dashboards | P1 |
| WhereThisSits | Closing main pane | Actual cross-series prior/current/next questions | P0 |
| SeriesBreadcrumb | Header when true series membership exists | Do not fabricate membership from reading path order | P0 |
| MobileContents | User-opened short sheet | Outline + thread navigation; no chatbot or app tab bar | P0 |
| FocusHost / NavigationController | One layout-level controller | Owns route-backed inspection and return stack | P0 |

These are responsibilities, not a mandate for one client framework component each. Reuse existing components where possible. Default to Astro/Markdown/native HTML; no LLM on render, scroll or navigation.

## Six canonical scenes

| ID / anchor | Exact latest filename | Meaning | Placement |
|---|---|---|---|
| T01 `thread-incident` | `registry_wave_incident_resolution_flow.png` | Source/registry fixed; separate copies stale | Immediately after incident is established |
| T02 `thread-deployment` | `registry_wave_from_source_to_outcome.png` | Same name, different bytes / records | After deployment explanation; anchor image |
| T03 `thread-use` | `registry_wave_presence_vs_behavior.png` | Instruction present is not instruction followed | Explicit conceptual branch |
| T04 `thread-drift` | `registry_wave_drift_across_five_days.png` | Original five-day discrepancy | Explicit return to original incident |
| T05 `thread-detection` | `registry_wave_detecting_silent_drift.png` | Byte comparison / dated drift-check method | Adjacent to detection discussion |
| T06 `thread-outcome` | `registry_wave_run_level_provenance_infographic.png` | Proposed loaded identity / evidence record | Outcome boundary, not proof of completion |

All remain inline and in this order. The focus route consumes the same selected asset. Do not recreate those figures from the ten mockup diagrams.

## Other supplied art

- `governed_cube_supply_chain_studio.png`: available real conceptual illustration, used in the prototype as an editorial hero. Crop still requires author review. The prototype does not regenerate Nick's portrait; it uses NM.
- `agentic_os_artifact_estate_before_and_after.png`: canonical closing synthesis, named but not available as bytes in this environment.
- `the_agentic_os_artifact_estate.png`: canonical final deep figure, also unavailable here.
- `registry_wave_thread_diagram_system.png`: internal style reference, not normal article content.
- `not_every_difference_is_drift.png`: optional candidate; prior semantic hold still applies. The new prototype uses a clearly labeled HTML comparison, not a silent replacement approved raster.
- `from_probabilistic_cognition_to_capability.png` / `from_capability_to_trusted_outcome.png`: earlier candidate illustrations; prior semantic holds are not cleared by this UX pass. Prefer actual WhereThisSits content for reading-path navigation.
- Optional topology/warehouse/city alternates: at most one editorial pair when needed, not evidence and not replacements for canonical figures.

The eight canonical technical images are unavailable **here**; this is not evidence they are absent from the user's local system. Local agents must locate exact filenames, pin hashes and inspect full-resolution text. No old variant may be renamed to impersonate a required file.

## Content field requirements

Thread record: ID, label/order, anchor, kind, title, narrative source, canonical figure reference, caption, long description, supported claim, limitations, related receipt IDs.

Artifact record: stable identity, display title, role/type, public source, version/revision only if supported, optional links and explicit status. Do not create “healthy,” “approved” or “running” from presence alone.

Receipt record: ID, title, source kind, claim support, limits, independently known event/recorded/verified dates, source locator/revision, capture state, publicability, related scene/paragraph anchors.

Context note: ID, section/scene scope, short title, one-sentence summary, optional concise body, optional link, dismissal policy. Never assembled by a model at reading time.

Asset record: exact filename, local availability, approved status, dimensions/hash when measured, semantic role, allowed placements, alt/caption source, supersedes/blocked-by references. A filename or generated composition is not clearance.

## Specific copy repairs

- Restore the manuscript taxonomy: Instruction, Tool, Context, Governance, Execution, Evidence. Do not adopt the mockup's replacement model/data ontology.
- Restore the six scene names. No Create/Publish/Review/Deliver rewrite.
- Keep “instruction present ≠ instruction followed”; do not replace with “presence ≠ provenance” or an implied gateway bypass.
- Delete fabricated metrics, implementation claims, source IDs and customer/production state from every visual.
- Delete “Governed means safe.” Governance makes decisions and scope inspectable; safety requires additional evidence.
- Keep the actual reading path and the planned state of E5.
- Use `nickmiethe.com` for site links; other generated `signal.system` addresses were not source-derived.
- Treat all new prototype paragraphs as layout copy, not an approved essay rewrite.
# IMAGE GUIDE — Registry Wave visual implementation

## 0. How agents should use this pack

There are intentionally multiple generations of imagery because they answer different questions.

- **Canonical composite mockups** answer: *How should the final page, modes, sidebar, and components appear together?*
- **Rich component direction** answers: *How polished and visually expressive can an individual component become?*
- **V2 prototype markups** answer: *How should state, navigation, return behavior, modes, and responsive interaction actually work?*
- **V1 prototype markups** answer: *What earlier layouts/states may still provide useful implementation context?*
- **Initial style variations** are mood/design exploration only.

Do not average conflicting references. Follow the precedence order in `README.md`.

### Content fidelity warning

Image-generation text is **not canonical copy**. Some older images deliberately or accidentally contain invented section names, artifact versions, receipts, metrics, product states, or labels. Copy styling and composition—not unsupported content. The current MDX, evidence records, and source-grounded handoff remain authoritative.

---

# 1. Canonical composite mockups — Tier A

These nine images are the **primary visual source of truth**.

| File | What it shows | Implementation authority |
|---|---|---|
| `01_essay-entry__canonical.png` | Hero/frontispiece, headline, metadata, flowing author card + Executive Signal, start of sticky Reading Companion | Canonical page entry, two-pane proportions, dark theme, type scale, flow-vs-sticky behavior |
| `02_first-scroll__canonical.png` | First substantive scroll, pull quote, active section marker, first inline figure; author/Executive Signal are gone | Canonical mid-essay sidebar state and section-marker treatment |
| `03_artifact-partial-context__canonical.png` | Partial-width composition, expanded Contextual Note, Editorial Table, active colored left rule | Canonical split-composition and contextual-note pattern |
| `04_thread-focus__canonical.png` | Focused thread inspection mode with only Running Example + Thread Overview in right rail | Canonical Thread Focus mode and return-to-essay affordances |
| `05_evidence-focus__canonical.png` | Evidence inspection mode: receipt, supported claim, limitations, evidence guide + index | Canonical Evidence Focus mode; not an essay-page section layout |
| `06_figure-viewer__canonical.png` | Enlarged figure modal over prior context, caption/long description and return behavior | Canonical FigureViewer/modal visual treatment |
| `07_managed-variation-inline__canonical.png` | Inline three-way comparison: Update / Reconcile / Deliberate Pin | Canonical inline explanatory comparison; **not** a separate mode/page |
| `08_conclusion-reading-path__canonical.png` | Closing figure, conclusion, `WhereThisSits`, previous/current/next question | Canonical essay conclusion and guided reading-path treatment |
| `09_mobile-modes__canonical.png` | Mobile essay entry, contents, thread focus, evidence focus | Canonical responsive visual language, not a native-app design |

## Canonical page-state rules visible in Tier A

- **Essay View:** primary pane + sidebar. Author and Executive Signal are normal-flow entry components; deeper in the essay only Reading Companion remains sticky.
- **Thread Focus:** focused inspection surface. Sidebar = Running Example + Thread Overview only. No author card, Executive Signal, or article TOC.
- **Evidence Focus:** focused inspection surface. Sidebar = Evidence Guide + Receipt Index only.
- **FigureViewer:** overlay/modal on top of the immediate prior context, and Close returns to that exact context.
- **Managed Variation:** remains inline in the essay.
- **WhereThisSits:** distinct from ordinary breadcrumb/series navigation; it explains the conceptual reading path.

---

# 2. Rich component direction — Tier B

These are **secondary visual references**, deliberately retained because they often contain richer card/detail treatments than the canonical composite set.

Use them for:
- card depth, glow, icon sizing, borders, spacing, mini-diagram polish;
- detailed Thread Overview and Running Example styling;
- ReceiptDisclosure/evidence-card richness;
- FigureViewer caption/control richness;
- typographic rhythm inside a component.

Do **not** use them to override:
- which components appear in the sidebar at a given scroll depth;
- whether something is a page versus a modal/focus surface;
- essay/thread/evidence information architecture;
- any factual copy, metrics, versions, availability states, or receipts;
- the final mobile navigation model.

### Files

- `01_essay-entry__rich-concept.png` — favored neo-editorial visual density and polish.
- `02_first-scroll__rich-concept.png` — rich first-scroll / diagram treatment; sidebar hierarchy is superseded.
- `03_artifact-partial-context__rich-concept.png` — detailed MediaSplit, table, badges; Executive Signal persistence is superseded.
- `04_thread-deployment__rich-concept.png` — useful Running Example detail card and technical figure polish; use canonical Thread Focus composition instead.
- `05_thread-use-overview__rich-concept.png` — strongest visual inspiration for Thread Overview / selected beat / hold state; canonical mode/sidebar rules supersede surrounding page.
- `06_managed-variation__rich-concept.png` — strong visual language for the three-path comparison; canonical semantics and copy supersede it.
- `07_evidence-receipts__rich-concept.png` — excellent Evidence/Receipt styling; **all fabricated receipt content is non-authoritative**.
- `08_figure-viewer__rich-concept.png` — detailed FigureViewer controls, caption treatment, previous/next; canonical return-state contract supersedes unsupported controls.
- `09_conclusion__rich-concept.png` — useful architecture-card treatment; invented next-essay and outcome copy must not be used.
- `10_mobile__rich-concept.png` — visual inspiration for mobile surfaces; robot assistant/app-tab concepts are superseded.

---

# 3. V2 prototype markups — Tier C

`03_V2_PROTOTYPE_MARKUPS/` is the rendered prototype family from the current experience specification. It is less visually lush than Tier B but is more trustworthy for **state and interaction semantics**.

Use it to resolve questions like:
- when the right rail changes;
- how Contextual Notes collapse/expand;
- what Thread Focus vs standalone thread looks like;
- how Evidence Focus returns;
- what mobile sheet/focus layouts do;
- how the thread sequence maps to essay anchors.

If a Tier-A image is visually ambiguous, consult V2 markups and `06_SUPPORTING_HANDOFFS/CURRENT-EXPERIENCE-SPEC.md`.

---

# 4. V1 prototype markups — Tier D

`04_V1_PROTOTYPE_MARKUPS/` contains the earlier full reading-experience wireframes. Keep them for layout archaeology and additional states, especially the six thread beats and earlier mobile experiments.

They are **not** current authority when they conflict with V2 or Tier A.

---

# 5. Initial style variations — Tier E

These four early explorations are mood/idea references only.

- Dark editorial variation — useful typography and section treatment.
- Light editorial variation — useful example of inline components and breathing room.
- Storyboard/dashboard variation — useful source for storyboard density, not final IA.
- Neo-editorial favorite variation — the visual ancestor of the current canonical system.

Agents may borrow aesthetic details only if they preserve Tier-A composition and V2 semantics.

---

# 6. Inline technical figures are a separate authority

The essay's semantic technical figures are not replaced by these page mockups. Follow `06_SUPPORTING_HANDOFFS/INLINE-FIGURE-IMAGE-USAGE-HANDOFF.md` for the latest named technical assets and placement rules.

That handoff requires the six thread images to remain in order and adjacent to corresponding prose, followed by the managed-variation comparison and closing estate figures when relevant. The mockups show **containers and presentation**, while the inline-figure handoff governs **which technical image is actually inserted**.

---

# 7. Agent implementation checklist

Before calling the visual implementation sufficient:

- [ ] Entry resembles Tier-A `01` in hierarchy, width balance, typography, and spacing.
- [ ] Author + Executive Signal scroll away; they do not persist deep into the article.
- [ ] Reading Companion is the only sticky essay sidebar surface at depth.
- [ ] Active section uses the colored left rule/number treatment without layout shift.
- [ ] Contextual Note is authored marginal context, not chat/AI generation.
- [ ] Dense figures can use primary-pane width and open in FigureViewer.
- [ ] Thread Focus contains only the focused beat plus Running Example + Thread Overview.
- [ ] Thread Focus has explicit `Back to essay` and `Read this scene in essay` semantics.
- [ ] Evidence Focus contains Evidence Guide + Receipt Index, not article TOC.
- [ ] Evidence content comes from real/source-grounded records; generated placeholders are not copied.
- [ ] Managed Variation is inline, not a modal/page.
- [ ] WhereThisSits remains a reading-path component, distinct from series/breadcrumb navigation.
- [ ] Mobile surfaces remain mobile web; no fabricated native-app tab bar/chatbot.
- [ ] FigureViewer returns to the immediate prior context and restores focus.
- [ ] Technical thread images follow the separate canonical image handoff.
- [ ] Actual current MDX/spec/evidence wins over text shown inside any generated mockup.

